{title: Going To California}
{artist: Led Zeppelin}
{key: F}

{c: Verse 1}
[F] [Em] [D] [C],        Spent my days with a woman unkind,
[F] [Em] [D] [C],        Smoked my stuff and drank all my wine.
[F] [Em] [D] [C],        Made up my mind to make a new start,
[F] [Em] [D] [C]
Going to california with an aching in my heart.
[F] [Em] [D] [C],        Someone told me theres a girl out there
[F] [Em] [C]
With love in her eyes and flowers in her hair.
[F] [Am] [C] [Am],        Took my chances on a big jet plane,
[F] [Am] [F] [C]
Never let them tell you that theyre all the same.
[F] [Em] [D] [C],        The sea was red and the sky was grey,
[F] [Em] [D] [C]
Wondered how tomorrow could ever follow today.
[F] [Em],        The mountains and the canyons started
[D] [C],        to tremble and shake
[F] [Em] [D] [C]
As the children of the sun began to awake.
[Cm],        Seems that the wrath of the gods
Got a punch on the nose and it started to flow;
[G7],        I think I might be sinking.
[Cm],        Throw me a line if I reach it in time
Ill meet you up there where the path,        [G7]
Runs straight and high.        [F] [Em] [D] [C]
To find a queen without a king;        [F] [Em] [D] [C]
They say she plays guitar and cries as she sings.
[F] [Em] [D] [C]
Ride a white mare in the footsteps of dawn
[F] [Em],        Tryin to find a woman whos never,
[D] [C],        never, never been born.
[F] [Am] [C]
Standing on a hill in my mountain of dreams,
[F] [Am],        Telling myself its not as hard,
[F] [C],        hard, hard as it seems.
